# What does NOT go into the published extension.
#
# vsce warns when a project has neither this file nor a `files` property, and it is right to: with
# neither, it packages whatever happens to be in the folder. Phase 119 wrote that risk down -
# "a packaging change could silently drop one" - and then left the folder to chance. This is the
# other half.
#
# Deliberately short. Everything the extension needs at runtime is in this folder and must stay in
# the package, so the safe default here is to exclude almost nothing. engine/test/extension.test.ts
# holds that: no pattern here may match a file the extension needs to run.

# Earlier builds. A .vsix inside a .vsix doubles the download for nothing.
*.vsix

# Type declarations are for editing this code, not for running it.
**/*.d.ts

# Editor and OS leftovers that are no part of the extension.
.vscode/**
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
